    "narrative": "For LawDog, the standout play is clearly **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who leads our lineup with a 70.29 efficiency score. He faces Leiter, and while the matchup is standard, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** gains a critical boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which historically inflates his stolen base probability\u2014a massive boon given our strategic overweighting of speed. Meanwhile, **Geraldo Perdomo** (62.79) serves as our most efficient mid-tier play; despite a lower batting order slot, he draws a favorable matchup against Littell (4.83 xERA), making him a high-floor asset who leverages the pitcher's vulnerability to drive value in the 5x5 categories.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involves **Gleyber Torres**, who sat at 46.83, just shy of the threshold to displace our lower-performing outfielders. While **Gleyber Torres** benefits from a strong park factor and a leadoff spot, the optimizer favored the platoon-neutral volume of **Tyler Freeman** (53.72), whose matchup in a hitter-friendly park outweighed the raw projection for **Gleyber Torres**. We are also keeping a close eye on **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Matt Chapman**; both benefit from the slow delivery of Brown, which significantly bolsters their stolen base potential despite the inherent risk of facing a decent arm. \n\nLooking at the remainder of the board, we are exercising caution with **Taylor Ward** (43.45) and **Gavin Sheets** (42.03), both of whom are hovering near our 40-point floor. **Taylor Ward** is particularly susceptible to the negative platoon variance against Fisher, and we will be monitoring the official lineups to ensure no late scratches emerge. We have opted to keep **Drew Gilbert** on the bench today, as his sub-40 score\u2014dragged down by a bottom-of-the-order assignment\u2014failed to meet our efficiency standards. With **Yainer Diaz** still sidelined on the IL, we are relying on our depth to carry us, though the heavy exposure to the Brown matchup via **Luis Arraez**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Matt Chapman** makes the early innings against his delivery speed the most pivotal window for our stolen base production.",
